  "reason": "Evidence: RNA is clearly the dominant signal (rna_only 0.485 vs image_only 0.208), and our best result (config_019, acc 0.639) uses PCA as the RNA encoder. The RNA encoder is the most important unexplored design axis—we have zero evidence on whether a learned encoder (scvi_n200) could improve upon PCA. Question: Does replacing pca_n2000 with scvi_n200 in the multimodal multiprofile pipeline (keeping resnet50, avgpool, weighted fusion fixed) improve performance? This is a single-variable change from our current best (config_019), cleanly isolating the RNA encoder effect in the setting most likely to yield the highest accuracy. Why this is the best next experiment: It directly tests the highest-impact unexplored axis in the configuration regime where we expect the best results, and the outcome (improvement or not) will guide all subsequent encoder choices across the remaining search space."
}

